sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch06-07> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The bulges that begin conjugation in algae such as Pleurocarpus and Mesocarpus, and the root-hair outgrowth of Equisetum spores, arise where surface tension is weakened, and these sites coincide with heavy concentrations of potassium salts, which disperse when the cell becomes symmetrical again.";
    dc:type "empirical-generalization";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Conjugation outgrowths and root-hairs arise at sites of potassium concentration";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter VI, “A Note on Adsorption”; topic “Potassium concentration and weakened tension”. Scope: conjugating zygnematacean algae, germinating Equisetum spores and other cells forming local outgrowths"
}
